sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User (Browser)
    participant Route as OpenShift Route<br/>443/TCP HTTPS (Edge TLS)
    participant UI as Streamlit UI<br/>8501/TCP HTTP
    participant BRoute as Backend Route<br/>443/TCP HTTPS (Edge TLS)
    participant Backend as FastAPI Backend<br/>8000/TCP HTTP
    participant Ollama as Ollama Sidecar<br/>11434/TCP HTTP
    participant HF as HuggingFace Hub<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant K8s as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Catalog as Model Catalog<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Arena as LMSYS Arena<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant AA as Artificial Analysis<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

    Note over User,AA: Flow 1: Deployment Planning Pipeline

    User->>Route: HTTPS/443 (TLS Edge)
    Route->>UI: HTTP/8501 (plaintext in-cluster)
    UI->>BRoute: HTTPS/443 (TLS Edge)
    BRoute->>Backend: HTTP/8000 (plaintext in-cluster)

    Note over Backend,Ollama: Step 1: Intent Extraction
    Backend->>Ollama: POST /api/chat<br/>HTTP/11434, No Auth
    Ollama-->>Backend: Structured Intent JSON

    Note over Backend: Step 2: Generate Specification
    Backend->>Backend: Transform intent → SLO spec<br/>(traffic, latency, cost targets)

    Note over Backend,HF: Step 3: Generate Recommendations
    Backend->>HF: GET model config<br/>HTTPS/443, HF_TOKEN
    HF-->>Backend: Model architecture info
    Backend->>K8s: LIST nodes<br/>HTTPS/6443, SA token
    K8s-->>Backend: GPU types from node labels
    Backend->>Backend: Score configs<br/>(quality × price × latency)

    Note over Backend: Step 4: Generate Deployment
    Backend->>Backend: Render KServe YAML<br/>(Jinja2 templates)

    Note over Backend,K8s: Step 5: Deploy to Cluster
    Backend->>K8s: kubectl apply<br/>HTTPS/6443, SA token
    K8s-->>Backend: Deployment status

    Backend-->>BRoute: JSON Response
    BRoute-->>UI: Recommendations + YAML
    UI-->>Route: Rendered UI
    Route-->>User: HTTPS Response

    Note over Backend,Catalog: Flow 2: Model Catalog Benchmark Sync

    Backend->>Catalog: GET /api/v1/models<br/>HTTPS/8443, Bearer token<br/>TLS (service-serving CA)
    Catalog-->>Backend: Benchmark data
    Backend->>Backend: Store in SQLite DB

    Note over Backend,AA: Flow 3: Quality Data Refresh

    Backend->>Arena: GET rankings<br/>HTTPS/443, No Auth
    Arena-->>Backend: Human preference data
    Backend->>AA: GET benchmarks<br/>HTTPS/443, AA_API_KEY
    AA-->>Backend: Automated benchmark data
    Backend->>Backend: Update local cache
